From 72a7024b2e04e464d5e911e876a5273457fe92cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcloud <bcloud@localhost>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 02:14:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zaya Q4NX: MUL_MAT_ID_Q4NX dispatch for stacked MoE experts

- ggml_mul_mat_id now routes Q4NX src0 to the new GGML_OP_MUL_MAT_ID_Q4NX
  (constructor result [tpe/n_tc*32, nselected, ntokens]).
- HRX2 dispatch_mul_mat_id_q4nx: per-(i,t) slices through the shared
  q4nx slice helper (per-expert tile copy -> q4nx dequant -> f32 mm cols=1).
- FIX: ids tensor is a strided VIEW of the argsort output (nb[1]=17*4);
  the dispatch copied it contiguously and picked the wrong expert for
  token>0 (second-best of token 0). Copy each token row at its real nb[1]
  stride into the packed q4nx_ids scratch.
- CPU backend rejects MUL_MAT_Q4NX / MUL_MAT_ID_Q4NX.
- logits corr vs F32 port: 0.9999999 (top1 9731, top5 identical); coherent
  generation on HRX20. Removed all debug dump scaffolding.
